# PRIV-19: An incognito session survives process death and stays incognito.
#
# launch-task, not launch-view. A fresh VIEW intent would carry the incognito
# extra itself and prove nothing about restoration. Resuming the task rebuilds
# MainActivity from its saved instance state, which is where vm.incognito comes
# back from, and that is the property under test.
describe Incognito survives process death and records nothing after restore

# Opens normal.pdf with the incognito extra, reads to page index 2, confirms the
# PdfRecord table stays empty, then backgrounds the app.
phase com.gitlab.mudlej.MjPdfReader.suite.privacy.Priv19ProcessDeathTest#phaseOneReadIncognitoAndBackground

kill-app
# Relaunch only after phase-two instrumentation has started, so its startup
# force-stop cannot erase the restored incognito activity.
launch-task-after-start

# Asserts the restored reader still shows the incognito indicator, and that
# reading on writes neither a PdfRecord row nor an annotation journal.
phase com.gitlab.mudlej.MjPdfReader.suite.privacy.Priv19ProcessDeathTest#phaseTwoAssertRestoredSessionIsStillIncognito
